RING\n8. CIVIL ENGINEERING\n9. THERMAL ENGINEERING\n10. MECHATRONICS ENGINEERING\n11. AUTOMATION AND CONTROL ENGINEERING\n12. ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEERING\n13. TELECOMMUNICATIONS ENGINEERING\n14. COMPUTER SCIENCE\n15. ECONOMICS AND MANAGEMENT\n16. EDUCATIONAL MANAGEMENT\n17. FOOD TECHNOLOGY\nARTICULATION\n1. Electrical and Electronics Engineering Technology\n2. Automotive Engineering Technology\n3. Construction Engineering Technology\n4. Printing Engineering Technology\n5. Machine Manufacturing Technology\nRESEARCH\nINTRODUCTION\nJOURNAL OF TECHNICAL EDUCATION SCIENCE\nSCIENTIFIC RESEARCH ACTIVITIES\nSTUDENTS' ACTIVITIES\nLECTURERS' ACTIVITIES\nOUTREACH\nENTERPRISE RELATIONS\nINTERNATIONAL RELATIONS\nALUMNI\nABOUT ALUMNI COMMUNITY\nALUMNI EVENTS\nHo Chi Minh City University of Technology and Education has been renamed Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology and Engineering (HCM-UTE) under Decision No. 2809/QĐ-TTg issued by the Prime Minister. Smart governnance & Empowering the HCM-UTE brand.\nNews\nHCMUTE Leadership Congratulates Medical Staff on Vietnamese Doctors' Day (February 27th)\nTác giả\n:\nOn the occasion of the 70th anniversary of Vietnamese Doctors' Day (February 27, 1955 – February 27, 2025), the Party Committee, University Council, and the Board of Rectors of Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology and Education (HCMUTE) visited and extended congratulations to the medical staff, officers, and employees working at the university's Medical Station on the morning of February 26, 2025.\nHCMUTE leaders visit and congratulate the Health Care Center\nDuring the meeting, Assoc. Prof. Dr. Le Hieu Giang, Deputy Secretary of the Party Committee and President of HCMUTE, expressed his gratitude and appreciation for the contributions of the Medical Station in providing healthcare services to faculty members, staff, and students. With dedication, responsibility, and continuous commitment, the medical team has played a crucial role in ensuring a safe and healthy learning and working environment. The university hopes that the medical staff will continue to uphold their professionalism, maintain their passion for the profession, and continuously enhance their expertise to remain a reliable support for the HCMUTE community.\nFollowing the visit to the Medical Station, Assoc.Prof.Dr.Le Hieu Giang and the university delegation also visited and congratulated the doctors at Thu Duc Regional General Hospital. This visit served as an opportunity for the university to acknowledge and appreciate the contributions of healthcare professionals in caring for the health of faculty, staff, and students.\nIn addition to the congratulatory activities, Assoc. Prof. Dr. Le Hieu Giang and the hospital's Board of Directors held discussions on potential collaborations in scientific research and the application of technology in medical practice. Both sides agreed to jointly develop technological products such as smart hospital beds, medical support robots, and drones to enhance healthcare services and optimize medical operations in the future.\nHCMUTE leaders visit and congratulate doctors at Thu Duc Regional General Hospital\nHCMUTE's Medical Station not only provides primary healthcare services but also plays a vital role in disease prevention, first aid, and medical consultation. With a dedicated staff and well-equipped facilities, the Medical Station is always ready to support faculty, staff, and students in any health-related situations.\nOthers\nStudy Abroad Opportunities in Taiwan for HCMUTE Students\n(24/02/2025)\nA-GRASS2025 CALL FOR PAPERS\n(24/02/2025)\nOpening Ceremony of the Distance Learning and Work-Study Programs (Bachelor’s Level) – Second Intake of 2024\n(22/02/2025)\nThe 7th Circuit and System Design Scientific Conference\n(21/02/2025)\nA New Milestone in Wood and Interior Technology Training: HCMUTE Partners with Canadian Wood Vietnam\n(14/02/2025)\nHCMUTE NEW YEAR GATHERING\n(11/02/2025)\nHCMUTE Youth Award 2025\n(05/02/2025)\nAssoc. Prof. Dr. Le Hieu Giang was appointed as President of HCMUTE\n(24/01/2025)\nHCMUTE and Lac Hong University Collaborate to Enhance Education and Scientific Research\n(21/01/2025)\nReunion Bus: Over 1,100 Students Return Home for Lunar New Year 2025\n(19/01/2025)\nComments\nFull Name:\n*\nEmail:\n*\nTitle:\n*\nCaptcha:\nRadEditor - HTML WYSIWYG Editor. MS Word-like content editing experience thanks to a rich set of formatting tools, dropdowns, dialogs, system modules and built-in spell-check.\nRadEditor's components - toolbar, content area, modes and modules\nToolbar's wrapper\nContent area wrapper\nRadEditor hidden textarea\nRadEditor's bottom area: Design, Html and Preview modes, Statistics module and resize handle.\nIt contains RadEditor's Modes/views (HTML, Design and Preview), Statistics and Resizer\nEditor Mode buttons\nStatistics module\nEditor resizer\nDesign\nHTML\nPreview\nRadEditor - please enable JavaScript to use the rich text editor.\nRadEditor's Modules - special tools used to provide extra information such as Tag Inspector, Real Time HTML Viewer, Tag Properties and other.\n*\nVisit month:\n10,445\nVisit total:\n316,896\nCopyright © 2013, HCMC University of Technology and Engineering\nAdd:\nNo 1 Vo Van Ngan Street, Thu Duc Ward, Ho Chi Minh City\nTel:\n(+84 - 028) 38968641 - (+84 -028) 38961333 - (+84 -028) 37221223\nFax:\n(+84 - 028) 38964922\nE-mail:\noia@hcmute.edu.vn"
